   $q$In paragraph 2, some dunes "tower hundreds of feet above the desert floor." What does "tower" mean in this sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"block the wind from passing","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"},{"text":"rise very high over something","is_correct":true},{"text":"lean to one side and fall","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"a tall, narrow building","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning-multiple-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$rise very high over something$q$, $q$Here "tower" is an action word, and the contrast with dunes "small enough to step over" plus the comparison "as tall as a skyscraper" show it means rise very high. A tall building is another meaning of "tower," but it does not fit as the verb in this sentence.$q$, 'draft', '86e3169b-1b47-55bb-a696-cd1f8a911efd')
