   $q$Paragraph 3 begins, "Ordinarily, freezing would be deadly for an animal." What does "Ordinarily" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"in most cases; usually","is_correct":true},{"text":"in a very short time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"},{"text":"in the forest; outdoors","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"},{"text":"almost never; rarely","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$in most cases; usually$q$, $q$The paragraph sets up a contrast: freezing usually harms animals, but "The wood frog survives because of a clever defense." The frog is the unusual case, so "ordinarily" means usually, not rarely.$q$, 'draft', '25a2c19d-abb7-5486-a0ac-7d3e712c08fb')
